[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial CyanogenMod 9 (Android 4.0.4 Ice Cream Sandwich) port for the Huawei Y210. It is built on the same legacy Qualcomm MSM7x27A stack as my CyanogenMod 7 port for this device and shares its fixes where the hardware is the same (Wi-Fi driver, GPS, RIL translation). The kernel is built from source.

[B]Device specs[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Device: Huawei Y210 (HUAWEI Y210-0151)
[*]Android version: 4.0.4 Ice Cream Sandwich (CyanogenMod 9)
[*]Kernel: Linux 2.6.38.6, built from source
[*]SoC: Qualcomm MSM7225A, 600 MHz (the ARM9 modem runs separately and reserves part of the RAM)
[*]RAM: 256 MB physical, ~178 MB usable by Android
[*]GPU: Adreno 200
[*]Screen: 320x480 HVGA, 32 bpp
[*]Wi-Fi: Atheros AR6003 (driver built from the AR6kSDK 3.1 sources)
[*]Bluetooth: Qualcomm Bahama (BlueZ)
[/LIST]

[B]Current status — Beta[/B]

Build: [B]PUT_ZIP_FILENAME_HERE[/B] | MD5: PUT_MD5_HERE

[COLOR="Red"][B]Read before flashing:[/B][/COLOR] please read the known issues. This is Ice Cream Sandwich on 256 MB of RAM: it works, but it is tighter than CM7. [B]There is no FM radio in this ROM.[/B]

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Boot & system:[/B] boots to the launcher after a clean flash; SurfaceFlinger, mediaserver and system_server stable
[*][B]Graphics:[/B] Adreno 200 for SurfaceFlinger and OpenGL apps (GPU benchmark: 18.4 FPS at the screen's resolution); hardware composer active
[*][B]Touchscreen and buttons:[/B] multitouch, physical and capacitive keys
[*][B]Backlight / LED / vibrator[/B]
[*][B]Telephony:[/B] SIM, operator registration, signal, IMEI, calls, SMS and HSPA mobile data; [B]SIM PIN lock[/B] (PIN prompt at boot, lock and change PIN)
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] scan, connect, DHCP, keeps the connection in deep sleep; driver built from source with Huawei's per-unit TX power calibration
[*][B]Wi-Fi hotspot:[/B] clients connect, get an address and browse over mobile data; normal Wi-Fi comes back when the hotspot is turned off
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] pairing, file transfer and Bluetooth tethering (NAP)
[*][B]Audio:[/B] speaker, headphones, microphone and calls
[*][B]Camera:[/B] preview and photo capture
[*][B]Accelerometer[/B] (the Y210 has no proximity or light sensor)
[*][B]GPS:[/B] the location engine connects to the modem; raw NMEA and correct dates (fixes shared with CM7)
[*][B]Storage / USB:[/B] /data, SD card and USB mass storage
[*][B]Memory:[/B] zram swap and ICS's own low-memory killer tuning
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]No FM radio:[/B] ICS has no FM framework for this chip and bringing over CM7's FM stack caused too many problems, so this ROM ships without FM. Use the CM7 ROM if you need the radio.
[*][B]App UIs are drawn in software:[/B] GPU-accelerated UI drawing (hwui) is turned off because with it every dialog came out garbled on the Adreno 200. OpenGL apps and games still use the GPU.
[*][B]GPS outdoor fix:[/B] not yet confirmed on this build (it is confirmed on CM7, same code)
[*][B]Camera video recording:[/B] not re-tested on this build
[*][B]Bluetooth audio (A2DP/headset):[/B] not tested yet
[*][B]Powering on with the charger connected:[/B] if the bootloader starts in charging mode, the phone stays on the boot logo. Turn it on with the USB cable disconnected.
[*][B]RAM is tight:[/B] Email, Exchange, the updater, DSP Manager and Voice Dialer can be disabled to free memory
[/LIST]

