[SIZE="4"][B]Changelog:[/B][/SIZE]

[B]PUT_BUILD_DATE_HERE[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Wi-Fi hotspot works[/B] (it never did on CM9): the hotspot option was hidden in Settings and the system had no support for this Wi-Fi chip in access point mode
[*][B]SIM PIN fixed:[/B] entering the PIN at boot always said "wrong PIN" because the request reached the modem driver empty and crashed it (no attempts were used); the "SIM network unlock" screen that could appear after the PIN is gone too
[*][B]GPS fixed:[/B] the location engine could not reach the modem because of a permission problem; raw NMEA and the 2019 GPS week rollover dates are fixed as on CM7
[*][B]Wi-Fi after a data wipe fixed:[/B] Wi-Fi did not turn on after a clean install; it now also applies Huawei's per-unit TX power calibration
[*][B]Garbled dialogs fixed:[/B] GPU-accelerated UI drawing is turned off (see known issues)
[*][B]Camera:[/B] photo capture works (the JPEG is now encoded in software)
[*][B]Wi-Fi driver built from source[/B] (AR6kSDK 3.1); keeps the connection in deep sleep like the stock driver
[*][B]Memory:[/B] 8 MB more RAM (two unused GPU memory reservations removed), zram swap, low-memory killer left to ICS
[*][B]Browser:[/B] fixed crashes on pages with SVG images when memory is low
[*][B]Bluetooth tethering (NAP)[/B] enabled in the kernel
[*][B]Signal bars fixed:[/B] the status bar always showed 0 bars and Settings showed -32767 dBm even with good coverage
[*][B]Claro Peru APNs[/B] included
[/LIST]

